From 5899ca8f144f4f95a53d2dfce25518d62d8f575d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AurisDSP <235008503+AurisDSP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 5 May 2026 20:37:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Apple Silicon (macOS arm64) dynarec port

Enable the native macOS ARM64 dynarec with Mach-O assembly, MAP_JIT,
and per-thread JIT write protection. Keep the allow-jit entitlement
requirement for Hardened Runtime hosts.

Give compilation, branch patching, and trampoline initialization their
own balanced write scopes. Cache flushing only synchronizes instructions;
unmapped compilation failures also restore executable state. Assert scope
imbalances instead of resetting or clamping the nesting depth.

Reserve Apple's x18 register and use IP0 for far-branch trampolines.
Preserve d8-d15 when switching libretro coroutines. Report MAP_JIT
allocation errors and return failed startup or reset to the frontend
without resuming a completed coroutine.

Keep non-Apple behavior and portable assembly symbol references intact.
